      "text": ["Curtain Road, Shoreditch.", "No sign on the door.", "Just a staircase, down."]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": ["Ade Fakile built the room.", "His father had run sound systems", "back home, in Ibadan, Nigeria."]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": ["He called his approach", "active darkness.", "No lights.", "Nothing to look at but the sound."]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": ["Two hundred microphones,", "every wall mapped.", "Below 49Hz, the room itself", "was bending the bass.", "He fixed it — foam, bass traps,", "the UK's first Funktion-One rig."]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": ["Thursday nights, a DJ named Hatcha", "cut dubplates from two teenagers", "who hung around a record shop in Croydon.", "Their names: Skream. Benga."]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": ["They called the night FWD>>.", "No one had a word", "for the music yet."],
      "sub": "Mala and Loefah played there too — before they built DMZ down the road in Brixton."
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": ["January 2015.", "The room closed", "without much noise."],
      "strobe": "Built for a frequency. Never needed a name.",
      "cta": "Save this."
